@input
vertex: vec3
uvs: vec2
normal: vec3

@output
uv: vec2

# Deliberately not element.fbvert's per-element pipeline (screen_rect math,
# image_uv's legacy 180-degree flip for textures loaded through the normal
# image path) - this always draws one fixed NDC-spanning quad
# (generate_quad(2.0, 2.0), see UIRenderer._composite_quad), so there's no
# per-element rect/window_size to convert from, and the texture it samples
# (the offscreen UI layer, ui/renderer.py's _ui_framebuffer) was rendered
# straight into via the same NDC convention as everything else in this
# engine, never through the image-loading path element.fbvert's `image_uv`
# is tuned for - see UIRenderer._composite_ui_layer's own docstring.
def main() -> void:
    VERTEX_POSITION = vec4(vertex.x, vertex.y, 0.0, 1.0)
    uv = uvs
